Ok I'm weirdly proud of this — my kid and I are building a chore tracker together and we got it working! It's a Flask app with one route that lists chores from a SQLite table. But now we want to add a checkbox so clicking it marks the chore done without reloading the page, and I have no idea where to start with that. Here's the route we have:

@app.route('/')
def index():
    rows = db.execute('SELECT id, name, done FROM chores').fetchall()
    return render_template('index.html', chores=rows)

Can you show us the fetch call on the front end and the little POST route on the back end? Keep it simple enough that a 12 year old can follow it please!
